# Next Steps (Planner → Coder/Runner/Reviewer/Author/Researcher)

Immediate directives from the Planner. Full directive text lives in
`plans/directives/<ID>.md` — one file per directive; **load only the
file(s) for your assigned directive**, not the whole directory. This file
holds the index, the current dispatch queue, and cross-cutting
riders/constraints. Pass narratives and rulings history: `plans/history.md`.
`plans/directives/<ID>.md` is gitignored (except `TEMPLATE.md`) and deleted
by the Reviewer at close-out — it's local working-session state, not the
durable record; that's `harness/status_history.md` (rule 3) and the
directive's tracker issue (rule 13, if a tracker is configured).

Update `coding/tasks_working.md` as you pick items up, and
`coding/tasks_finished.md` + a work record per rule 12 (its reference
pasted next to it) when done — see the `[DONE]` definition in
`harness.md`. Ping back via `plans/suggestions.md` if a directive is
ambiguous or you hit a blocker — do not silently reinterpret scope.
Also keep `harness/status.md`'s "Directive status" table current (rule 3) —
that's the live per-directive owner/state view; this table's queue rows are
the static spec, not the live state.

## Directive ID convention

`D<NN>`, one file per directive in `directives/<ID>.md`.

